flutter_edge_ai (patch_c_api.sh section 33, part 2): text LoRA sessions, a
backport of LiteRT-LM PR #2508 (leehack, "Support text LoRA sessions through
ResourceManager", head f51fe329, Apache-2.0) onto v0.20.0 plus upstream
4d4fd6e5 (part 1, patches/litert_lm_zero_lora_buffers_4d4fd6e5.patch).

Public source, v0.20.0 and main (59977885): ResourceManager::
CreateContextHandler builds the ModelAssets of a not yet loaded text LoRA and
returns InvalidArgumentError("Lora is not supported."); the LLM executor has no
LoadLoRA/UseLoRA. Upstream 4d4fd6e5 (main, after the v0.20.0 fork) binds zero
LoRA buffers in RunSignature behind `bool bound_active_lora = false;`, under the
comment "Tracks whether the internal-only LoRA manager bound an active adapter
so OSS builds (where the block below is stripped) still bind zero buffers."

From #2508: LoadLoRA/UseLoRA on LlmExecutorBase, implemented on the
compiled-model executor through LoraManager; forwarding in LockedLlmExecutor;
the context's lora_id kept through CloneContext and re-selected by
RestoreContext; SessionConfig keeps the LoRA paths; ResourceManager loads a
text LoRA once per id (on v0.20.0's scoped-file keys and lock order, as its
audio branch does); #2508's ResourceManager tests, on v0.20.0's
FakeLlmExecutor.

Ours, where upstream has nothing public: the active LoRA is bound in
RunSignature, in the place of the stripped block, for every signature (prefill
as well as decode; #2508 bound decode only) through
LoraManager::GetLoRABuffers(signature); SaveContext and the ProcessedContext
RestoreContext keep and select the lora_id too (they postdate #2508). The
active LoRA is the LoraManager's current ID, and UseLoRA passes nullopt to the
manager. This follows the behaviour of Google's shipped v0.20.0 library
(litert-lm-api 0.20.0, macOS arm64), read from its machine code for
interoperability: RunSignature binds GetLoRABuffers(signature) when the manager
has a current ID, else BindZeroLoRABuffers; LoadLoRA creates the manager on
the "decode" signature; UseLoRA defers to the manager; both RestoreContext
overloads select the context's lora_id; ResourceManager loads the adapter
under a lock where v0.20.0 returns "Lora is not supported."; the NPU executor
refuses. A model without LoRA inputs takes an adapter without effect there
too; litertlm_dart refuses one from the bundle header instead. The NPU
executor keeps the base LoadLoRA, which returns Unimplemented.

